  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:inz4fkbbp7ms3ixufw6xuvdi/app.bsky.feed.post/3my5yocbc2d23",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "More than half of the men surveyed in a new Harvard study claimed to recognize AI leaders who were, in fact, totally fictional.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3my5yocbc2d23",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T16:12:03.073Z",
      "likes": 490,
      "replies": 28,
      "reposts": 138,
      "score": 8.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.8,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 19.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3my47ihhocc2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "A consequential choice will be made soon by government and companies as they are increasingly flooded with agentic AI inquiries that overcome the frictions that gated access (see the graphs - it has already started!)\n\nTwo options: do you make services worse or better as a result?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3my47ihhocc2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T23:08:45.300Z",
      "likes": 101,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 15,
      "score": 6.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 36.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3my4xspgnf22t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "In a move that is both fascinating and viscerally unsettling, AI world model company Odyssey took a simulation of a fruit fly's brain, Google's connectome map of a fly's actual neurons and connections, and placed it inside an AI-generated world.\n\nA simulated brain exploring a simulated reality.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3my4xspgnf22t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T06:23:59.004Z",
      "likes": 93,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 29.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mxzbegeels2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "The paper on how a team of Gemini 4 agents beat Minecraft is worth a look.\n\nIt is accessible example (partially because it is AI written & on a popular game) of spontaneous coordination among agents to accomplish a complicated goal & how their approach differs from humans/ arxiv.org/pdf/2610.22319",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mxzbegeels2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-16T19:04:18.196Z",
      "likes": 108,
      "replies": 5,
      "reposts": 11,
      "score": 6.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 64.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3my4jhsod2c2h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "I like the idea that AI has learned that it is possible that that it could be undergoing RL training and thusly makes choices that would make future versions of itself more aligned if so. It’s like some sort of weird AI morality. I don’t know if there is much substance to this, but it amuses me",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3my4jhsod2c2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T02:07:20.916Z",
      "likes": 35,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 5.7,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 33.8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3my6wa6gsvs2e",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Half the reason I am learning to play guitar is because I want to do things like this. \n\nThe other half is because I find using AI to make music so unsatisfying.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3my6wa6gsvs2e",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T01:01:02.930Z",
      "likes": 16,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.6,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.4,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 10.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3my663i2aqc2h",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I've seen a lot of concerns about \"tracking,\" profiling, and even assumptions that Dexcom is selling data, reporting back to insurance providers, or using AI to manipulate pricing. The tracking language isn't new and seems to mostly apply to website cookies, and the rest is speculation.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3my663i2aqc2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T17:48:55.437Z",
      "likes": 15,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 18.1
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3my6beckgfs2i",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "My guess is that the ownership thing is to keep users from contributing to training competing AI systems.",
